      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is utterly bleak to feel that individual actions are futile against such massive systemic failure, and recognizing the severity of the threat while feeling helpless is a very heavy burden to carry. While the \"death sentence\" analogy is frightening, history also shows that collective human ingenuity can adapt, innovate, and build resilience even in the darkest times. Sometimes, finding meaning is exactly about bearing witness to the struggle and refusing to give up, hoping to change the math for a tiny few.",
      "source": "target",
